win32u: mouse tracking follows the capture window, so a captured drag gets no WM_MOUSELEAVE

The window the mouse is "in" for TrackMouseEvent is the window that receives the mouse messages: while the mouse is
captured, the capture window, client area, whatever is under the cursor. ReactOS, which mirrors Windows here,
hands IntTrackMouseMove the capture window with HTCLIENT (co_IntProcessMouseMessage), so a window that holds the
capture never gets WM_MOUSELEAVE; the leave comes after the capture is released. get_mouse_window() looked up the
window under the cursor instead, so a captured drag that crossed the window's edge was sent WM_MOUSELEAVE mid-drag.

Lightroom Classic: "you can only scroll on the scrollbar with the mouse directly on top of it if clicking and
dragging. The moment the mouse hovers outside of the scrollbar it stops scrolling". Its panel scroll bars are
ScrollBar-class windows tracked by Lightroom itself; trace on the nested desk: capture held by the bar throughout,
then LEAVECHECK track=bar under=(nil) -> WM_MOUSELEAVE posted, and the thumb stopped.

Measured, same 100-px drag of the Develop panel's thumb with the pointer drifting sideways:
  sideways 0 / 30 / 90 px: thumb moves 100 / 100 / 100 (NEUTRON_CAPTURE_TRACKING=0: 100 / 22 / 16).
The hover highlight still clears after a drag released off the bar (the leave arrives once capture is gone), and
dragging the Masks panel still works.

Kill switch NEUTRON_CAPTURE_TRACKING=0.

--- a/dlls/win32u/input.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/input.c
@@ -1673,12 +1673,39 @@
     }
 }
 
+/* NEUTRON capture-tracking (2026-10-15): the window the mouse is "in" for TrackMouseEvent is the window that gets
+ * the mouse messages, which while the mouse is captured is the capture window, client area -- whatever is under the
+ * cursor. Windows (and ReactOS, which mirrors it: co_IntProcessMouseMessage hands IntTrackMouseMove the capture
+ * window with HTCLIENT) therefore never sends WM_MOUSELEAVE to a window that holds the capture; the leave comes once
+ * it is released. Here the leave check looked up the window under the cursor, so a captured drag that crossed the
+ * window's edge got WM_MOUSELEAVE mid-drag. Lightroom Classic's panel scroll bars (ScrollBar class, tracked by
+ * Lightroom itself) stop on it: "you can only scroll on the scrollbar with the mouse directly on top of it if
+ * clicking and dragging. The moment the mouse hovers outside of the scrollbar it stops scrolling". Trace: capture
+ * held by the bar, LEAVECHECK under=(nil) -> WM_MOUSELEAVE posted. Kill switch NEUTRON_CAPTURE_TRACKING=0. */
+static BOOL neutron_capture_tracking(void)
+{
+    static int on = -1;
+    if (on < 0)
+    {
+        const char *e = getenv( "NEUTRON_CAPTURE_TRACKING" );
+        on = e ? (e[0] != '0') : 1;
+        ERR( "neutron-gateresolved: NEUTRON_CAPTURE_TRACKING = %d (%s)\n", on, e ? "environment" : "default" );
+    }
+    return on;
+}
+
 static HWND get_mouse_window( HWND hwnd, INT *hittest, POINT *ret_pos, struct mouse_tracking_info *tracking )
 {
     POINT pos;
-    HWND ret;
+    HWND ret, capture;
 
     NtUserGetCursorPos( &pos );
+    if ((capture = get_capture()) && neutron_capture_tracking())
+    {
+        *hittest = HTCLIENT;
+        *ret_pos = pos;
+        return capture;
+    }
     ret = window_from_point( hwnd, pos, hittest, FALSE );
     if (ret && ret == tracking->last_mouse_message_hwnd)
     {
